Package: PNC
Type: Package
Title: Phylogenetic Signal in Niche-Related Traits Across Ecological
        Communities
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-8-19
Authors@R: c(person(given = "Yan", family = "He", email = "heyaneco@163.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),person(given = "Yu", family = "Xia", role = "aut"),person(given = "Rui", family = "Yang", role = "aut"),person(given = "Lingfeng", family = "Mao", role = "aut"))
Maintainer: Yan He <heyaneco@163.com>
Description: Provides a standardized workflow for evaluating phylogenetic signal in niche-related functional traits within ecological communities. The package integrates functional trait data across major taxonomic groups and implements Pagel's lambda and Blomberg's K for individual species pools and multiple communities. It also evaluates the sensitivity of Pagel's lambda inference to incomplete trait data using simulation-based paired comparisons. These tools facilitate empirical assessment of phylogenetic structure in ecological traits and its robustness to trait-data incompleteness. Methods build on Blomberg et al. (2003) <doi:10.1111/j.0014-3820.2003.tb00285.x> and Münkemüller et al. (2012) <doi:10.1111/j.2041-210X.2012.00196.x>.
